<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; color:#000000; bEditID:r3st1; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial">{!Contact.FirstName},</font><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Thank you for your interest in the Department of Physics at Arizona State University.</font></div><div><span style="font-family: arial;"><br></span></div><div><span style="font-family: arial;">Please be sure to review our </span><a href="https://physics.asu.edu/" style="font-family: arial;">website</a><span style="font-family: arial;">, which contains contact information for all of our faculty members (<a href="https://physics.asu.edu/content/people">People link</a>) and lists the application requirements and procedures (<a href="https://physics.asu.edu/phd/apply">PhD Students/How to Apply</a>).&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: arial;">Most of the application process is completed online, but official transcripts and GRE/TOEFL scores must be submitted to the Graduate College as explained under the "<a href="https://physics.asu.edu/phd/apply">How to Apply"</a> link. Note that both the general and subject (physics) GRE exams are required.</span></div><div><span style="font-family: arial;"><br></span></div><div><span style="font-family: arial;">To receive full consideration for the fall semester, your application and all supporting materials, including reference letters, should be received by <b>January 31</b>.&nbsp;</span></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Many students inquire about the selectivity of our PhD program. The averages are different for domestic (D) and international (I) students. Typically, we receive 120 applications (D=40, I=80), make 50 offers (D=25, I=25), and receive 25 acceptances (D=15, I=10).&nbsp;<br><br></font></div><div><font face="arial"><b>Approximate average metrics for the incoming cohort</b></font></div><div><font face="arial">GPA = 3.4 with the following GRE scores: Quantitative (D</font><span style="font-size: 12pt;">=75%, I=85%), Verbal (D=70%, I=60%), Written (D=50%, I=25%), Physics Subject (D=40%, I=75%).</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Regardless of averages, I can assure you that each file is reviewed carefully to assess items beyond scores and grades. ASU requires international students to have minimum TOEFL scores of 515 (PBT), 213 (CBT), or 83 (iBT). At the department level, we look for scores about 15% above these minima, since language skills are critical for teaching assistant positions.</span></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">We have excellent programs to offer at ASU. I hope you will complete an application and I wish you all the best as you begin your graduate degree.</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Sincerely,</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial">Jeff Drucker</font></div><div><font face="arial">Director of Graduate Admissions</font></div><div><font face="arial">Department of Physics</font></div><div><font face="arial">Arizona State University</font></div><div><font face="arial"><a href="mailto:jeff.drucker@asu.edu">Jeff.Drucker@asu.edu</a></font></div><div><font face="arial">480-965-9658</font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial"><br></font></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>